## [0.21.2] - 2026-07-20

**Bug-fix maintenance release (V2 LTS).** Two correctness fixes backported from
the 3.x `main` line.

### Fixed

- **Denied / missing `UPDATE` and `merge()` now raise instead of silently
  no-opping (#139, backport of #135).** On a table protected by row-level
  `PERMISSIONS`, a write the current user is not allowed to make — or one
  targeting a row that no longer exists — makes SurrealDB return an *empty*
  result (zero affected rows), not an error. Previously `save()` on a persisted
  instance and `merge()` discarded that result and returned `self`, so a denied
  update was indistinguishable from a successful one and callers could silently
  lose data while reporting success. A denied/missing update now raises
  `SurrealDbError`, mirroring the existing create-path guard, across every
  non-deferred write path: plain `client.merge()`, the `SurrealFunc`
  raw-`UPDATE` path, the complex-nested-data SET-clause path, and WebSocket
  transactions. A new `BaseTransaction.defers_results` property keeps
  HTTP-transaction behaviour unchanged — their per-statement results only exist
  at `commit()`, so the guard is skipped there. (Known limitation: denial
  *inside* an HTTP transaction remains undetectable at statement time.)
- **`istartswith` / `iendswith` are now actually case-insensitive (#138,
  backport of #134).** They previously compiled to the same SurrealQL as the
  case-sensitive `startswith` / `endswith`, so e.g. `name__istartswith="ali"`
  did not match `"Alice"`. Both the field and the value are now lowercased
  (mirroring `icontains`), and both raise `TypeError` for non-string values.

### Changed

- **Version bump to 0.21.2** — `pyproject.toml`, `surreal_orm/__init__.py`,
  `surreal_sdk/__init__.py`, `surreal_sdk/pyproject.toml`.

---

## [0.21.1] - 2026-06-09

**Security maintenance release (V2 LTS).** No library code changes vs 0.21.0 —
runtime behaviour is identical. Reaffirms the `cbor2 <6` pin and tags the CI/docs
fixes that landed after 0.21.0.

### Security

- **`cbor2` stays pinned `<6` — rejected the 6.x widening.** Dependabot proposed
  relaxing the requirement to `cbor2>=5.9.0,<7` (PR #117), which would re-allow
  cbor2 **6.x** on this branch. 6.x changed the custom-tag encoding and breaks the
  SurrealDB **2.x** CBOR RPC path the bundled SDK relies on; the 6.x compatibility
  fix only landed on `main` (the 3.x line) and was **not** backported here. The
  security floor (`cbor2>=5.9.0`, avoiding the vulnerable 5.6–5.8 range) is already
  in place, so #117 added no security value and was closed.
- **Dependabot now ignores `cbor2` `semver-major` updates on the `v2` target**
  (config lives on the default branch). This stops the `<7` widening from being
  re-proposed against this LTS branch.

### Changed

- **CI: v2 LTS releases are no longer marked GitHub "Latest" (#113)** — the
  "Latest" badge belongs to the active 3.x `main` line; a v2 release must not
  outrank a higher-versioned main release on the releases page.
- **Docs: V2 retirement threshold clarified (#114)** — this branch is retired once
  [SurrealDB-ORM-lite](https://github.com/EulogySnowfall/SurrealDB-ORM-lite)
  reaches **v0.40.0 (beta)**.
- **Version bump to 0.21.1** — `pyproject.toml`, `surreal_orm/__init__.py`,
  `surreal_sdk/__init__.py`, `surreal_sdk/pyproject.toml`.

---

## [0.21.0] - 2026-06-06

### Deprecated

- **V2 LTS branch deprecated in favor of [SurrealDB-ORM-lite](https://github.com/EulogySnowfall/SurrealDB-ORM-lite).**
  The official SurrealDB Python SDK v2 has matured, so the bundled custom SDK is no longer needed for the
  SurrealDB 2.x line. SurrealDB-ORM-lite continues to support SurrealDB 2.x on top of that official SDK.
  This branch will only receive **security and bug fixes** until SurrealDB-ORM-lite reaches **v0.40.0 (beta)**,
  after which it will be retired.
  - Importing `surreal_orm` now emits a `DeprecationWarning` pointing to SurrealDB-ORM-lite.
  - README carries a deprecation banner; the package stays `Development Status :: 4 - Beta` while still maintained.

### Security

- **Dependency upgrades — 21 known CVEs cleared across 7 packages** (`aiohttp`, `idna`, `urllib3`, `pytest`,
  `python-dotenv`, `pygments`, `tornado`). `uv.lock` refreshed.
  - **`aiohttp>=3.14.0`** — runtime floor raised so published clients also get the patched version
    (CVE-2026-34513..34525, CVE-2026-22815, CVE-2026-34993, CVE-2026-47265, and others).
  - **`cbor2>=5.9.0,<6`** — floor raised to avoid vulnerable 5.6–5.8 releases; capped below 6.0 since
    cbor2 6.0 may break the SurrealDB 2.x custom-tag encoding this branch relies on.

### Fixed

- **Transient `401` under host clock skew (issue #101)** — Backported from `main`. The SDK HTTP layer
  (`surreal_sdk/connection/http.py`) now re-mints the JWT and retries with a short backoff when a request
  fails with a `401` caused by a freshly-minted token whose `nbf` claim is momentarily in the future
  (e.g. WSL2 backward clock jumps). Signin credentials are retained on `HTTPConnection` to enable re-minting;
  a `401` without retained credentials is still raised immediately as a genuine auth failure.
- **Transaction rollback test on SurrealDB 2.6.x** — On 2.6.x, `SELECT` from a non-existent table returns an
  `ERR` ("table does not exist") rather than an empty OK result. After a successful rollback the table is
  never created, so `test_transaction_rollback_no_records` now treats that `ERR` as valid proof that no
  records were persisted.

### Changed

- **Version bump to 0.21.0** — `pyproject.toml`, `surreal_orm/__init__.py`, `surreal_sdk/__init__.py`,
  `surreal_sdk/pyproject.toml`.
- **`publish.yml` tag filter** — added `v0.21.*` so the PyPI publish workflow triggers for the 0.21.x
  LTS line (previously only `v0.20.*`).
- **Validated against SurrealDB v2.6.5** — `.surrealdb-version` and Docker Compose pinned to v2.6.5;
  README "Tested with" updated. Full unit suite plus 362 integration tests pass on v2.6.5.
- **Docs synced with `main`** — `SECURITY.md` adopts the two-branch supported-versions policy; "last updated"
  dates refreshed in `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/roadmap.md`.

---

## [0.20.0] - 2026-03-10

### V2 LTS Branch — SurrealDB 2.X Maintenance

This release establishes the **V2 LTS maintenance branch** for SurrealDB 2.X backward compatibility.
The `main` branch now targets SurrealDB 3.X (version 0.30.x), while the `v2` branch (version 0.20.x)
continues to receive security updates and bug fixes for SurrealDB 2.X users.

### Added

- **V2 LTS branch setup** — Protected `v2` branch with its own CI/CD pipeline, separate from `main`.
- **SurrealDB 2.X Version Monitor** — Daily automated workflow (`surrealdb-security.yml`) that:
  - Checks for new SurrealDB 2.X releases (ignores 3.X+)
  - Runs full unit + integration test suite against new versions
  - Auto-creates PRs targeting the `v2` branch when tests pass
  - Bumps ORM version and creates tagged releases for security patches
  - Creates GitHub issues when tests fail for manual investigation
- **CI targeting V2** — `ci.yml` now triggers on pushes/PRs to the `v2` branch.
- **Dependabot auto-merge for V2** — `dependabot-automerge.yml` merges into `v2` branch and bumps patch version.
